{
  "scope_note": "I covered pages 1-35, extracting project, funding, target, decision and event statements about JETP Indonesia and the domestic/international case studies. I left out navigation, acronyms, acknowledgements of individuals, global and macroeconomic statistics not tied to a partnership project, general recommendations and their tables, and figure/chart-only values, as out of scope.",
  "statements": [
    {
      "page": 3,
      "quote": "The development of this paper was made possible through funding from the government of Canada to the JETP of Indonesia, through the CEFIM Programme, and with additional funding from the government of Denmark.",
      "label": "funding from the government of Canada to the JETP of Indonesia",
      "classification": "register_allocation",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": null,
        "funder": "the government of Canada",
        "implementer": "the JETP of Indonesia",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "additional funder", "value": "the government of Denmark"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 8,
      "quote": "Under its Enhanced Nationally Determined Contribution (NDC), Indonesia aims to cut emissions by 31.89% unconditionally and 43.2% conditionally by 2030.",
      "label": "Indonesia aims to cut emissions by 31.89% unconditionally and 43.2% conditionally by 2030",
      "classification": "target",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": "by 2030",
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": "Indonesia",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": []
    },
    {
      "page": 8,
      "quote": "Key milestones include the issuance of Government Regulation No. 79 of 2014 on National Energy Policy, which set ambitious renewable energy targets at 23% of the national primary energy mix by 2025 and 31% by 2050.",
      "label": "Government Regulation No. 79 of 2014 on National Energy Policy",
      "classification": "decision",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": "2014",
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "targets set", "value": "23% of the national primary energy mix by 2025 and 31% by 2050"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 8,
      "quote": "Subsequent commitments, such as the ratification of the Paris Agreement through Law No. 16 of 2016",
      "label": "the ratification of the Paris Agreement through Law No. 16 of 2016",
      "classification": "decision",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": "2016",
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": []
    },
    {
      "page": 14,
      "quote": "The 2023 quota-based net-metering regulation requires PLN approval by region, limiting participation.",
      "label": "The 2023 quota-based net-metering regulation",
      "classification": "decision",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": "2023",
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": "PLN",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": []
    },
    {
      "page": 14,
      "quote": "Installed capacity of ~100 MW in 2023, well below the 3.6 GW target by 2025.",
      "label": "3.6 GW target by 2025",
      "classification": "target",
      "fields": {
        "amount": "3.6 GW",
        "date": "by 2025",
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "installed capacity", "value": "~100 MW in 2023"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 14,
      "quote": "Around 700–800 MW of capacity is installed, mainly solar and small hydro.",
      "label": "Around 700–800 MW of capacity is installed, mainly solar and small hydro",
      "classification": "quota",
      "fields": {
        "amount": "700–800 MW",
        "date": null,
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": []
    },
    {
      "page": 14,
      "quote": "Regulation MEMR 1/2023 enables private generators to sell directly to industrial clients using PLN’s network.",
      "label": "Regulation MEMR 1/2023",
      "classification": "decision",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": "1/2023",
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": []
    },
    {
      "page": 17,
      "quote": "For instance, Sebira Island’s hybrid mini-grid generated a yearly net profit of USD 103 700 and created 51 jobs, while West Waru’s system achieved an energy cost of USD 0.054 per kWh with a 6-year payback period, reducing CO2 emissions by 67.2%.",
      "label": "Sebira Island’s hybrid mini-grid",
      "classification": "named_item",
      "fields": {
        "amount": "USD 103 700",
        "date": null,
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "jobs created", "value": "51 jobs"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 21,
      "quote": "Vietnam’s rooftop solar portfolio led by GreenYellow successfully consolidated over 45 small-scale projects into a single investment vehicle, demonstrating how aggregation can lower transaction costs and attract institutional capital.",
      "label": "Vietnam’s rooftop solar portfolio led by GreenYellow",
      "classification": "named_item",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": null,
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": "GreenYellow",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "projects consolidated", "value": "over 45 small-scale projects"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 21,
      "quote": "In Indonesia, the government’s dedieselisasi programme, which seeks to replace over 5 000 diesel generators in remote locations, offers an opportunity to apply a similar approach.",
      "label": "the government’s dedieselisasi programme",
      "classification": "target",
      "fields": {
        "amount": "over 5 000 diesel generators",
        "date": null,
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": "the government",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": []
    },
    {
      "page": 18,
      "quote": "Currently, the ministerial regulation on hybrid power plants is being drafted.",
      "label": "the ministerial regulation on hybrid power plants",
      "classification": "submission",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": null,
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": []
    },
    {
      "page": 25,
      "quote": "In addition to the National Budget of the Ministry of Energy and Mineral Resources, the Special Allocation Fund for Renewable Energy Infrastructure (DAK-IET) provides targeted allocations from the national budget to certain provinces, regencies, and cities to fund priority activities.",
      "label": "the Special Allocation Fund for Renewable Energy Infrastructure (DAK-IET)",
      "classification": "heading",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": null,
        "funder": "the national budget",
        "implementer": "certain provinces, regencies, and cities",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": []
    },
    {
      "page": 28,
      "quote": "Launched in 2022 as a partnership between the British Embassy Jakarta and PT Sarana Multi Infrastruktur (PT SMI), and facilitated through the UK's MENTARI programme, the Viability Gap Fund (VGF) has successfully mobilised private investment in renewable energy projects nearing financial viability.",
      "label": "the Viability Gap Fund (VGF)",
      "classification": "event",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": "2022",
        "funder": "the British Embassy Jakarta",
        "implementer": "PT Sarana Multi Infrastruktur (PT SMI)",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "facilitated through", "value": "the UK's MENTARI programme"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 28,
      "quote": "With an initial grant of approximately GBP 1.1 million (IDR 21 billion), the VGF has leveraged around GBP11.3 million (IDR 209.6 billion) in additional financing, a leverage ratio of over 1:10.",
      "label": "an initial grant of approximately GBP 1.1 million (IDR 21 billion)",
      "classification": "register_allocation",
      "fields": {
        "amount": "GBP 1.1 million (IDR 21 billion)",
        "date": null,
        "funder": "the VGF",
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "financing leveraged", "value": "around GBP11.3 million (IDR 209.6 billion)"},
        {"name": "leverage ratio", "value": "over 1:10"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 28,
      "quote": "The fund operates on a blended finance model and contributes up to 20% of a project's total value, though actual contributions have ranged between 6% and 15%.",
      "label": "contributes up to 20% of a project's total value",
      "classification": "quota",
      "fields": {
        "amount": "up to 20% of a project's total value",
        "date": null,
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "actual contributions range", "value": "between 6% and 15%"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 28,
      "quote": "One notable example is three hydropower projects with a combined capacity of 7.1 MW and total investment value of IDR 210 billion, developed by PT Brantas Energi, which received viability gap support through the VGF in 2023.",
      "label": "three hydropower projects with a combined capacity of 7.1 MW",
      "classification": "named_item",
      "fields": {
        "amount": "IDR 210 billion",
        "date": "2023",
        "funder": "the VGF",
        "implementer": "PT Brantas Energi",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "combined capacity", "value": "7.1 MW"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 28,
      "quote": "The VGF grant kicked in, covering approximately 10% of project costs. This was critical in closing this funding gap, enhancing the debt service capacity and unlocking PT SMI loan financing for developers (JETP, 2025[25]).",
      "label": "The VGF grant kicked in, covering approximately 10% of project costs",
      "classification": "register_allocation",
      "fields": {
        "amount": "approximately 10% of project costs",
        "date": null,
        "funder": "the VGF",
        "implementer": "developers",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "loan financing unlocked", "value": "PT SMI loan financing for developers"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 29,
      "quote": "In line with this, MENTARI and PT SMI signed a Memorandum of Understanding in November 2024 to establish a renewable energy Trust Fund, which aims to formalise and expand VGF-type interventions.",
      "label": "a Memorandum of Understanding in November 2024 to establish a renewable energy Trust Fund",
      "classification": "event",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": "November 2024",
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": "MENTARI and PT SMI",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": []
    },
    {
      "page": 29,
      "quote": "To bridge this gap and reduce inequality, the Government of Indonesia, the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP), and the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) launched the ACCESS programme in 2020.",
      "label": "the ACCESS programme",
      "classification": "event",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": "2020",
        "funder": "the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA)",
        "implementer": "the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP)",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "co-launcher", "value": "the Government of Indonesia"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 29,
      "quote": "By 2024, it had deployed solar energy solutions in 22 villages across four provinces, serving households, schools, clinics, and micro-enterprises.",
      "label": "deployed solar energy solutions in 22 villages across four provinces",
      "classification": "event",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": "By 2024",
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": "it",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "villages", "value": "22 villages across four provinces"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 31,
      "quote": "In 2014-2015, in Muara Enggelam, a government grant of IDR 3.9 billion (USD 250 000) under the Special Allocation Fund enabled the construction of a 35 kWp solar grid, later expanded to 45 kWp in 2020, while the Deutsche Gesellschaft für Internationale Zusammenarbeit (GIZ) provided technical assistance on entrepreneurship and community empowerment.",
      "label": "a government grant of IDR 3.9 billion (USD 250 000) under the Special Allocation Fund",
      "classification": "register_allocation",
      "fields": {
        "amount": "IDR 3.9 billion (USD 250 000)",
        "date": "2014-2015",
        "funder": "the Special Allocation Fund",
        "implementer": "Muara Enggelam",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "technical assistance provider", "value": "Deutsche Gesellschaft für Internationale Zusammenarbeit (GIZ)"},
        {"name": "capacity", "value": "a 35 kWp solar grid, later expanded to 45 kWp in 2020"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 31,
      "quote": "In contrast, Watukarere’s solar grid, funded by a Physical Special Allocation Fund, faced operational and financial challenges due to inadequate management, lack of technical capacity, and limited productive energy use. The grid, initially designed to serve 160 households, now operates at half capacity, with many residents unable or unwilling to pay electricity fees due to low incomes.",
      "label": "Watukarere’s solar grid",
      "classification": "named_item",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": null,
        "funder": "a Physical Special Allocation Fund",
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "designed capacity", "value": "160 households"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 31,
      "quote": "Mata Redi’s mini-grid represents a comprehensive donor-led model. Funded by the UK’s MENTARI program, the project integrates infrastructure development, vocational training, and long-term maintenance agreements. With 95 kWp of solar capacity, it powers households and public facilities while fostering productive energy uses, such as agricultural processing and women’s empowerment initiatives.",
      "label": "Mata Redi’s mini-grid",
      "classification": "named_item",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": null,
        "funder": "the UK’s MENTARI program",
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "capacity", "value": "95 kWp of solar capacity"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 31,
      "quote": "In Treweng, a communal solar grid funded by the Ministry of Villages provided initial electricity access but lacked sufficient capacity for productive uses. Subsequent grid expansion by PLN in 2020 replaced the earlier infrastructure, rendering it obsolete due to insufficient operational funding.",
      "label": "a communal solar grid funded by the Ministry of Villages",
      "classification": "named_item",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": "2020",
        "funder": "the Ministry of Villages",
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "subsequent grid expansion", "value": "Subsequent grid expansion by PLN in 2020"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 32,
      "quote": "In 2023, Special Allocation Fund (DAK) of IDR 88 billion was received by MEMR to support the renewable energy pilot project in Sumba. This project encompasses 21 solar panel infrastructure in 21 villages.",
      "label": "Special Allocation Fund (DAK) of IDR 88 billion was received by MEMR to support the renewable energy pilot project in Sumba",
      "classification": "register_allocation",
      "fields": {
        "amount": "IDR 88 billion",
        "date": "2023",
        "funder": "Special Allocation Fund (DAK)",
        "implementer": "MEMR",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "scope", "value": "21 solar panel infrastructure in 21 villages"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 32,
      "quote": "This is a continuation of previous DAK activities in energy sector which was suspended in 2019 due to the local government’s limited capacity to manage the asset.",
      "label": "previous DAK activities in energy sector which was suspended in 2019",
      "classification": "event",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": "2019",
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": []
    },
    {
      "page": 32,
      "quote": "Launched in 2005 as a global initiative by Germany and Netherlands, EnDev has focused on rural electrification through decentralised renewable energy solutions. In Indonesia, EnDev was operational from 2009 to 2019, implementing over 1 034 renewable energy mini grids in remote areas, including micro-hydro and solar PV systems.",
      "label": "EnDev was operational from 2009 to 2019",
      "classification": "event",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": "from 2009 to 2019",
        "funder": "Germany and Netherlands",
        "implementer": "EnDev",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "mini grids implemented", "value": "over 1 034 renewable energy mini grids"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 33,
      "quote": "The program provided electricity to over 295 000 people, 3 800 social institutions, and 2 900 rural businesses.",
      "label": "provided electricity to over 295 000 people",
      "classification": "count",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": null,
        "funder": null,
        "implementer": "The program",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "beneficiaries", "value": "over 295 000 people, 3 800 social institutions, and 2 900 rural businesses"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 33,
      "quote": "The Asian Development Bank (ADB) pilot-tested two such community-owned, off-grid micro-hydropower plants in the Philippines, located in Getsemane, Agusan del Sur, and Dalupan, Davao del Sur.",
      "label": "two such community-owned, off-grid micro-hydropower plants in the Philippines",
      "classification": "named_item",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": null,
        "funder": "The Asian Development Bank (ADB)",
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "locations", "value": "Getsemane, Agusan del Sur, and Dalupan, Davao del Sur"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 34,
      "quote": "Another significant ADB-supported project is the 30-kW Dhostekhor Khola Micro Hydropower Pilot Project in Nepal, designed as a model to expand access to clean electricity in rural and remote areas.",
      "label": "the 30-kW Dhostekhor Khola Micro Hydropower Pilot Project in Nepal",
      "classification": "named_item",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": null,
        "funder": "ADB",
        "implementer": null,
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": [
        {"name": "capacity", "value": "30-kW"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 34,
      "quote": "Another was the hybrid solar PV mini-grid in Cobrador Island, the Philippines, where the community was represented by an electric cooperative (ADB, 2021[31]).",
      "label": "the hybrid solar PV mini-grid in Cobrador Island, the Philippines",
      "classification": "named_item",
      "fields": {
        "amount": null,
        "date": null,
        "funder": "ADB",
        "implementer": "the community",
        "speaker": null
      },
      "other": []
    }
  ]
}
